{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Agreed UI design scope",
      "text": "Service quote accepted by Nara, buyer, and Dimas, designer in Indonesia.\nProject: interface design for the fictional LumaNest mobile app.\nFee: EUR 480, payable through PayPal.\n\nAgreed deliverables:\nDesign a mobile app home screen.\nDesign a mobile app profile screen.\nDesign three mobile app onboarding screens.\nProvide an interactive prototype linking the home and profile screens.\n\nDelivery is to be made as exported screen images and, for the prototype, a shareable interactive file. The fee covers the deliverables listed above; development and app store submission are not included."
    },
    {
      "title": "Design handover note",
      "text": "From: Dimas\nTo: Nara\nProject: LumaNest mobile app UI\n\nI have delivered the following exported images in the handover folder:\n- home-screen.png: completed home screen design.\n- profile-screen.png: completed profile screen design.\n- onboarding-1.png: completed first onboarding screen design.\n- onboarding-2.png: completed second onboarding screen design.\n\nThe folder contains no third onboarding screen. No interactive prototype was delivered. The images are static exports, so the home and profile screens cannot be navigated between in them. Please review the supplied designs and let me know whether you would like to discuss the outstanding work."
    },
    {
      "title": "Post-delivery chat",
      "text": "14:05 Nara: I received the four image exports. The home and profile designs both open correctly.\n14:08 Dimas: Thanks for checking. Those are the final designs for those two screens.\n14:12 Nara: I can also see two onboarding designs, but the third one is not in the folder.\n14:16 Dimas: Correct. I have not delivered the third onboarding screen.\n14:19 Nara: I could not find a prototype either. Are the images meant to link together?\n14:23 Dimas: No, they are static images. I did not deliver the interactive prototype.\n14:27 Nara: Understood. Let's discuss how to finish the remaining work."
    }
  ],
